ck if you're impacted here: 【98†https://github.com/orlyjamie/tailslop†github.com】\nL451: \nL452: 【96†theonejvo】\nL453: \nL454: •\nL455: \nL456: 【99†14h ago】\nL457: \nL458: It seems like a nothing burger. Based on my testing, none of this impacts a default vanilla install. 【100†https://x.com/theonejvo/status/2114417998408933418?s=20†x.com】\nL459: \nL460: 【101†Image: media poster†preview.redd.it】\nL461: \nL462: 【102†illhaveubent】\nL463: \nL464: •\nL465: \nL466: 【103†16h ago】\nL467: Why does Tailscale not participate in bug bounty programs like other tech companies? It seems irresponsible to not tackle these vulnerabilities preemptively, especially for a software product that sits on the network edge.\nL468: \nL469: 【104†punkgeek】\nL470: \nL471: •\nL472: \nL473: 【105†6h ago】\nL474: \nL475: Irresponsible would be publicly posting the vulnerability without contacting the vendor so they have time to patch before disclosure. (Bounty or not)\nL476: # More posts you may like\nL477: \nL478: Related posts\nL479: \nL480:   * 【106†Every time I paste shell commands or multi-line scripts, I get a warning ⚠️】\nL481: \nL482: 【107†r/Ghostty】 •\nL483: \nL484: 【106†Every time I paste shell commands or multi-line scripts, I get a warning ⚠️】\nL485: \nL486: upvotes · comments\nL487: \nL488: * * *\nL489: \nL490:   * 【108†Guide to preventing the most common enterprise social engineering attacks】\nL491: \nL492: 【109†r/netsec】 •\nL493: \nL494: 【108†Guide to preventing the most common enterprise social engineering attacks】\nL495: \nL496: upvotes · comments\nL497: \nL498: * * *\nL499:   * 【110†How Tailscale helped discover a 16+ year old SQLite WAL-Reset bug】\nL500: \nL501: 【111†r/programming】 •\nL502: \nL503: 【110†How Tailscale helped discover a 16+ year old SQLite WAL-Reset bug】\nL504: \nL505: upvotes · comments\nL506: \nL507: * * *\nL508: \nL509:   * 【112†I audit AI-generated codebases. Here are the 5 security issues I find in almost every single one.】\nL510: \nL511: 【113†r/VibeCodersNest】 